    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d343">

                <pb facs="0324" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.48/1171: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-09T20:00:00-04:00">September 9, 1937—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>335. Reference Department’s 250, August 20, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d343-f1"/> regarding accommodation for British refugees at Manila.
                    Department has received an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> from the
                    British Embassy which states in substance that His Majesty’s Government in the
                    United Kingdom desire to assure the United States Government that funds will be
                    made available for expenses that may be incurred in the Philippines as a result
                    of the reception there of British refugees.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
